#nav-bookmarks.doc-content 
    h1 insertBookmarks();
    .definition  Insert a user's list of bookmarked items.
        br
        |This function gets included in all pages automatically and is defined in 
        span.path /public/javascripts/contents/nav.js
        |. 
        img(src='images/docs/nav-bookmarks-1.png' style='display:block;margin-top:20px;height:309px;')
    h2 DOM Elements 
    p Insert the following base element to your pug file to add the bookmarks list in your page:
    p.code #bookmarks 
    p You can also use another id, but you will then have to pass the right name using the 'id' parameter (see section Parameters). Add the following optional classes to this DOM element to adjust the contents display:
    p 
        table.row-hovering 
            tr 
                th Class Name 
                th Description
            tr 
                td surface-level-[1..5]
                td Add the UI classes surface-level-1 through surface-level-5 to adjust the background color of the element 

    h2 Parameters
    p Various parameters can be provided using a JSON object as shown below. Note that all parameters are optional.
    p.code insertBookmarks({ 'size' : 'xs'});
    p   
        table.parameters.row-hovering
    h2 Examples 
    p   
        table.row-hovering 
            tr 
                th Code 
                th Screenshot 
                th Application 
            tr 
                td.code 
                    span.indent-1 insertBookmarks({
                    span.indent-2 'workspacesIn'  : ['82'],
                    span.indent-2 'header'        : true,
                    span.indent-2 'headerLabel'   : 'Pinned Problem Reports'
                    span.indent-1 });

                td
                    img(src='images/docs/nav-bookmarks-2.png' style='height:192px;')
                td -

    h2 Events 
    p You can override the following functions in your code to adjust the default behavior.
    p 
        table.row-hovering
            tr 
                th Function 
                th Event 
                th Parameters 
            tr 
                td insertBookmarksDone(id, data)
                td Once the list of bookmarks items got inserted, this function will be called. It will also be executed after a manual refresh of the list.
                td 
                    ul 
                        li id = id of the parent div element (i.e. bookmarks)
                        li data = data of given REST API call in PLM
            tr 
                td clickBookmarkItem(elemClicked, e) 
                td This function is invoked when a user clicks a tile in the list of bookmarks. It opens the given record in PLM per default.
                td elemClicked = jQuery element of the given tile which got clicked by the user; e = click event
